{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0318","billNumberShort":"H.B. 318","billNumberLong":"HB0318","fileNumber":"2026FL0549","shortTitle":"Agency Fee Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"CHRISKJ","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Christofferson, Kay J.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"VICKEEJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Vickers, Evan J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies provisions related to budgetary procedures.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>requires that, before billing another state agency for a good or service, an internal service fund agency provide specified rate data to the Governor's Office of Planning and Budget and to the Office of the Legislative Fiscal Analyst;<hr><ltbullet>requires an internal service fund agency to annually report the actual costs and revenue for each rate, fee, or other amount charged during the preceding fiscal year;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits a fee agency from charging a fee unless the fee agency provides specified fee data to the Governor's Office of Planning and Budget and to the Office of the Legislative Fiscal Analyst;<hr><ltbullet>requires a fee agency to annually report the actual costs and revenue for each fee charged during the preceding fiscal year; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Christine R. Gilbert","fiscalAnalyst":"Steven M. Allred","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/24/2026","trackingID":"PEMVSTOGNK","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-21 14:29:52.660","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research a